        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(google-meet): force English UI when reusing existing Chrome tabs",
        "body": "Closes #103385\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where `openclaw googlemeet join --mode transcribe` (and `googlemeet.create`) with the Chrome transport would silently fail when an existing Meet tab was rendered in a non-English UI. The plugin's browser automation matches English aria-labels and page text (\"Join now\", \"Turn off microphone\", etc.), so a reused tab opened in Japanese or another locale would never reach `inCall: true`, enable captions, or return a meeting URL, with no error pointing at the UI language.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe code already forced `?hl=en` when opening a **new** tab, but the reuse path only focused the existing tab. Now, after focusing a reused tab in both the join (`chrome.ts`) and create (`chrome-create.ts`) flows, the plugin navigates the tab to the English variant of its URL before running any DOM-matching automation. If the tab is already using English UI, the URL is unchanged and no navigation is issued.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers with Google accounts or browser profiles that default Meet to a non-English language can now rely on `googlemeet join`/`create` with the Chrome transport without manually appending `?hl=en` to the URL. Join/status behavior becomes language-independent for reused tabs.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Focused tests:\n  - `pnpm test extensions/google-meet/index.test.ts -- --run` → 116 passed\n  - `pnpm test extensions/google-meet/index.create.test.ts -- --run` → 10 passed\n  - `pnpm test extensions/google-meet/src/transports/chrome-browser-proxy.test.ts -- --run` → 4 passed\n- Added regression coverage:\n  - Join reuse test asserts `/navigate` to the English URL when the existing tab lacks `hl=en`.\n  - Join reuse test asserts no `/navigate` when the existing tab already has `hl=en`.\n  - Create reuse test asserts `/navigate` to the English URL when the existing tab lacks `hl=en`.\n  - Create reuse test asserts no `/navigate` when the existing tab already has `hl=en`.\n- No live Chrome browser proof is included because this environment lacks Crabbox/Blacksmith access; the fix is exercised entirely by focused unit tests plus the existing `forceMeetEnglishUi` helper.\n",
        "branch": "fix/google-meet-force-english-ui-on-reuse",
